type: software
title: "cmsopen: end-to-end analysis of CMS open data"
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - given-names: "Cyril"
    family-names: "Nadar"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/TODO"  # TODO: set it in templates/release_metadata.json
abstract: "cmsopen is an open-source Python library for analysing CMS NanoAOD open data: it selects muons, forms opposite-sign pairs, computes invariant masses and fits the Z and J/psi resonance peaks. Sample: benchmark 20 pre-registered files, observed 20 files (met). Fit adequacy: benchmark chi2/ndf <= 2.0; observed 1.518 for the Z (met) and 3.028 for the J/psi (not met). Observed peak positions, without momentum-scale corrections and so not mass measurements: 90.9000 GeV (Z) and 3.09332 GeV (J/psi). Unofficial analysis of CMS Open Data, not a CMS result."
keywords:
  - "CMS"
  - "open data"
  - "particle physics"
  - "Z boson"
  - "J/psi"
  - "invariant mass"
  - "NanoAOD"
  - "Python"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CyrilCquark/cmsopen"
